You are implementing process variable management and task execution for a BPMN engine.

Rules:
- Process variables live in a ConcurrentHashMap<String, Object> per instance — always in memory for active instances
- Variable reads and writes for active instances NEVER touch disk — only flush to storage on instance completion or checkpoint
- Service tasks are executed inline when sequential — a chain of N tasks runs as a single uninterrupted operation
- External task workers poll via REST (long-poll pattern) or register as Spring beans with @ServiceTask annotation
- Use virtual threads for all task worker execution — never a shared thread pool for I/O-bound workers
- Task locking: use optimistic locking with a version counter, not synchronized blocks
- Gateways (XOR, AND) are resolved inline with no async boundary
- Never use @Async on the hot execution path — virtual threads handle concurrency natively
